      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Payne estate, once a 42,000‑square‑foot Gilded Age mansion, now serves as Marist College’s Raymond A Rich Leadership Institute.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Park%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After a decade of abandonment, the former Payne mansion and school were converted in 2015 into Hudson House, a luxury vodka distillery, hotel, and event space.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Park%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "West Park’s Hudson River frontage is largely protected by Scenic Hudson or owned by religious orders, making homes scarce and highly sought after.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Park%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Church of the Ascension Holy Trinity, built in 1842 for an Episcopal congregation, sits at 1585 Route 9W in West Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
